  "notes": "Composed of {輸|ゆ} (transport) + {血|けつ} (blood). Used as both a noun and a suru verb.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {輸血|ゆけつ}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{受|う}ける→受ける：01215_ukeru⟧: to receive a blood transfusion\n- {輸血|ゆけつ}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to transfuse blood / to give a transfusion\n- {輸血|ゆけつ}⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦{必要|ひつよう}→必要：00846_hitsuyou⟧: a transfusion is necessary\n- ⟦{大量|たいりょう}→大量：03112_tairyou⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧{輸血|ゆけつ}: a large transfusion\n- {輸血|ゆけつ}パック: blood transfusion bag\n\nRELATED MEDICAL 〜{血|けつ} TERMS:\n- ⟦{献血|けんけつ}→献血：16161_kenketsu⟧: blood donation\n- ⟦{採血|さいけつ}→採血：11074_saiketsu⟧: blood drawing, taking blood\n- ⟦{出血|しゅっけつ}→出血：11735_shukketsu⟧: bleeding\n- ⟦{止血|しけつ}→止血：19782_shiketsu⟧: stopping bleeding\n- ⟦{血液型|けつえきがた}→血液型：03053_ketsuekigata⟧: blood type",
